WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.230 --> 00:00:01.470
- A lot of you have been asking me

00:00:01.470 --> 00:00:04.060
what I've been up to lately,
so here's a quick update,

00:00:04.060 --> 00:00:07.170
as well as some behind the
scenes of my latest LA trip.

00:00:07.170 --> 00:00:08.155
Boom!

00:00:08.155 --> 00:00:09.813
Bow-wop! (laughing)

00:00:09.813 --> 00:00:12.730
(upbeat pop music)

00:00:13.980 --> 00:00:16.130
- [Radio Announcer] We
have a very special guest.

00:00:16.130 --> 00:00:17.330
A very good looking

00:00:17.330 --> 00:00:20.310
and a very smart guest, Doctor Mike.

00:00:20.310 --> 00:00:21.790
You might know him from Instagram.

00:00:21.790 --> 00:00:23.730
He has 2.5 million followers.

00:00:23.730 --> 00:00:24.563
- Thank you.

00:00:24.563 --> 00:00:27.750
- Why is hot water better and
why is a cold shower better?

00:00:27.750 --> 00:00:29.570
- Warm water is better because cold water

00:00:29.570 --> 00:00:31.900
shunts blood away from your stomach,

00:00:31.900 --> 00:00:33.430
so you don't absorb it as readily.

00:00:33.430 --> 00:00:36.110
- You're very knowledgeable,
very visually appealing,

00:00:36.110 --> 00:00:37.770
and we really appreciate you being here.

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:39.258
- Thank you so much.
- All right.

00:00:39.258 --> 00:00:42.175
(upbeat pop music)

00:00:44.970 --> 00:00:46.740
- While I was in LA, I was able to catch

00:00:46.740 --> 00:00:48.390
up with some of my old friends.

00:00:48.390 --> 00:00:51.200
In fact, my buddy Marco, he
was there at the same time

00:00:51.200 --> 00:00:52.410
on a business venture.

00:00:52.410 --> 00:00:53.540
We were able to catch up.

00:00:53.540 --> 00:00:56.281
He introduced me to his
adorable dog, Titan.

00:00:56.281 --> 00:00:59.198
(upbeat pop music)

00:01:01.825 --> 00:01:05.075
(smooth hip-hop music)

00:01:07.740 --> 00:01:11.160
In 2015, during my little
viral moment of fame,

00:01:11.160 --> 00:01:13.770
the first nationally syndicated TV show

00:01:13.770 --> 00:01:16.400
that invited me on was The Doctors Show

00:01:16.400 --> 00:01:18.130
and they invited me on, obviously,

00:01:18.130 --> 00:01:20.900
as "Instagram's sexiest
doctor" as a guest.

00:01:20.900 --> 00:01:23.030
(crowd cheers)

00:01:23.030 --> 00:01:25.360
And it was a really great
experience, I was able to talk

00:01:25.360 --> 00:01:27.740
about how I'm passionate about medicine.

00:01:27.740 --> 00:01:30.380
Talk a little bit about
my past and my future.

00:01:30.380 --> 00:01:33.079
And, now, to be invited
to the same program

00:01:33.079 --> 00:01:36.470
as a host, as a co-host
with these doctors that have

00:01:36.470 --> 00:01:40.660
been doing this for 10 years
is such an amazing opportunity.

00:01:40.660 --> 00:01:42.860
It really makes me feel
like the whole situation

00:01:42.860 --> 00:01:44.140
has come full circle.

00:01:44.140 --> 00:01:45.990
Originally, I came on as a guest.

00:01:45.990 --> 00:01:47.720
Now, I'm coming out as a co-host.

00:01:47.720 --> 00:01:49.930
It shows that I wasn't just popular

00:01:49.930 --> 00:01:52.400
for 15 minutes of fame
because of my looks.

00:01:52.400 --> 00:01:55.230
I have a medical message that
I wanna get out there to you.

00:01:55.230 --> 00:01:57.760
I wanna have fun with
medicine and I think because

00:01:57.760 --> 00:02:00.790
you've been so receptive and
shown me so much support,

00:02:00.790 --> 00:02:03.150
it's because of that I'm
able to get an opportunity

00:02:03.150 --> 00:02:03.983
like co-hosting The Doctors Show.

00:02:03.983 --> 00:02:07.206
(smooth hip-hop music)

00:02:10.960 --> 00:02:14.182
I was also invited to
the premiere of a movie,

00:02:14.182 --> 00:02:17.120
"Flatliners", and it's movie
based on medical students

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:19.752
who were trying to kill
themselves and bring them back

00:02:19.752 --> 00:02:22.010
in order to experience the afterlife.

00:02:22.010 --> 00:02:24.640
- I would like you to stop my heart.

00:02:24.640 --> 00:02:26.723
You give it one minute and
then you bring me back.

00:02:26.723 --> 00:02:27.556
(beeps)

00:02:27.556 --> 00:02:28.440
- The one thing I'll
say about the movie is

00:02:28.440 --> 00:02:31.130
that it totally surprised
me because I thought

00:02:31.130 --> 00:02:33.590
it was gonna be maybe a
little science fiction

00:02:33.590 --> 00:02:36.991
about medical students and
how medicine can give you

00:02:36.991 --> 00:02:40.030
a peek into the afterlife,
when in reality,

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:41.890
it turned out to be a scary movie.

00:02:41.890 --> 00:02:44.460
I'm a baby when it comes to
that, so half of the movie,

00:02:44.460 --> 00:02:46.140
I was watching like this.

00:02:46.140 --> 00:02:48.630
So, if you saw me in the
theater, don't judge me.

00:02:48.630 --> 00:02:52.200
Alrighty, so we're headed to
Ricky Dillon's house right now.

00:02:52.200 --> 00:02:53.600
We're gonna surprise you with a collab

00:02:53.600 --> 00:02:56.050
next week or maybe the
week after, so stay tuned.

00:02:57.030 --> 00:03:00.280
The most unique part of my
trip was that I was able to do

00:03:00.280 --> 00:03:03.200
something I've never done
before and that's meet this

00:03:03.200 --> 00:03:05.360
adorable pig named Luna.

00:03:05.360 --> 00:03:07.740
Ricky was able to show
me how smart this pig is.

00:03:07.740 --> 00:03:10.300
How if you call the pig,
the pig actually comes over.

00:03:10.300 --> 00:03:13.780
I'm totally jealous because
I can't have a pet pig.

00:03:13.780 --> 00:03:16.790
New York City has an
explicit ban on pet pigs.

00:03:16.790 --> 00:03:19.957
(sad trombone blares)

00:03:20.871 --> 00:03:24.121
(smooth hip hop music)

00:03:25.280 --> 00:03:27.690
There are new media outlets
out there like Cheddar,

00:03:27.690 --> 00:03:30.850
Mashable, Instant, and I do
visit some of those outlets

00:03:30.850 --> 00:03:32.710
because I believe that they are doing

00:03:32.710 --> 00:03:34.183
a great job for society.

00:03:34.183 --> 00:03:36.420
They're taking the
concepts and the formats

00:03:36.420 --> 00:03:38.100
of a traditional news network,

00:03:38.100 --> 00:03:39.440
but making it a little bit more

00:03:39.440 --> 00:03:42.440
millennial friendly and I
could totally get behind that.

00:03:42.440 --> 00:03:44.950
Because if I could have
my message reach anybody,

00:03:44.950 --> 00:03:47.340
it's millennials, the younger generation.

00:03:47.340 --> 00:03:49.610
The biggest impact you
can make on your health

00:03:49.610 --> 00:03:52.153
is in your age group, so take listen.

00:03:52.153 --> 00:03:55.403
(smooth hip hop music)

00:03:57.010 --> 00:03:58.100
